content.text:
I found three more places with the same mistake, all in one file, [OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Workspace/OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp). Each one records the selected printer with `Preset::label(false)` instead of `Preset::name`. That label is what the combo box shows. When the printer has unsaved edits, it is the name with `"* "` in front, for example `"* Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle"`. No preset has that name, so the model can't use it to set up the printer, and saved printer facts get stored under two different keys. I found this by reading the code; I haven't reproduced it in the app yet.

## Where a label is used instead of the name

**1. "Printer settings…" in the header menu** ([PrinterMenu.cpp:174](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/PrinterMenu.cpp:174)). This is the one you hit. It passes the header's display name, which is the printer's model name when a stock profile is selected ([SetupCommands.cpp:99](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/SetupCommands.cpp:99)). The printer conversation doesn't find it among your saved printers, so it switches to adding a printer.

**2. The printer name the model sees on every turn** ([OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:273](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Workspace/OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:273)). `setup.printer_preset` is set from `get_selected_preset().label(false)`. It goes to:
- the context sent to the model with each message ([OpenAIResponsesAgent.cpp:37](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/OpenAIResponsesAgent.cpp:37));
- the `workspace_inspect` result ([ToolResults.cpp:551](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ToolResults.cpp:551));
- the page ([AgentHost.cpp:471](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentHost.cpp:471));
- the print history record ([AgentHost.cpp:1360](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/AgentHost.cpp:1360), [ManufacturingHistory.cpp:46](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ManufacturingHistory.cpp:46)).

If the model copies that value into `printer_setup`, the lookup at [OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:513](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Workspace/OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:513) fails with `unknown_preset`.

**3. The configured printer, which is also the key for saved printer facts** ([OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:1361](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Workspace/OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:1361)). Printer facts are things the person has told the agent about their machine. `configured.preset` becomes the fact key `"preset:<label>"` ([ToolResults.cpp:213](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ToolResults.cpp:213)). Facts confirmed while the printer has unsaved edits are stored under `"preset:* …"`. Once the edits are saved or discarded, they are looked up under `"preset:…"` and don't come back, and the reverse happens too.

**4. The printer that the `printer_setup` preview shows** ([OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:530](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Workspace/OrcaWorkspaceAdapter.cpp:530), used at line 614). `resulting.preset` is also a label. It feeds the same fact key when facts are read and written during setup ([ToolExecutionCoordinator.cpp:1713](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.cpp:1713), [:1741](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.cpp:1741)). It is only a problem when the target is the currently selected printer and it has unsaved edits.

Why the value gets a `"* "` prefix: upstream `Preset::label()` puts the "modified" marker in front of the name (Preset.cpp:767). The app sets that marker to `"* "` (GUI_App.cpp:7729). And `PresetCollection::update_dirty` sets `is_dirty` on the selected preset (Preset.cpp:3393), not just on the edited copy.

## Similar case where code doesn't do the lookup

"Filament settings…" ([FilamentMenu.cpp:462](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/FilamentMenu.cpp:462)) puts the filament's short display name into the chat note, for example "Bambu PLA Basic" when the preset is "Bambu PLA Basic @BBL A1M". No code looks that up. But the model reads the note and could pass the short name to a settings tool, which would fail to find it.

## Checked and correct

These all pass the real preset name:
- the Home screen's printer actions, which pass ids built from preset names;
- the header menu's "Other printers" rows;
- the filament menu rows and the filament chip;
- `NamedPrinters`, `HostLaneReader` and `OrcaPrinterBackend`;
- the web pages, which send ids, never names.

## Fix

The fix for 2 to 4 is to use `.name` at those three lines. The project summary already reports unsaved edits separately (`presets_dirty`), so nothing is lost. I'd like to reproduce the `"* "` value first in a separate copy of the app with its own data folder, not your running instance: edit a printer setting without saving, then read `workspace_inspect`. After that I'd make the change. Should I go ahead?

